---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";

const example = `[
  {
    "path": "/home/me/.agents/wt/fix-login",
    "repo": "/home/me/code/app",
    "branch": "fix-login",
    "safe": true,
    "facts": {
      "dirty": 0,
      "unchecked_files": 0,
      "unpushed": 0,
      "merged": "content",
      "size_bytes": 482113536
    }
  },
  {
    "path": "/tmp/scratch/old-app",
    "repo": "/home/me/code/old-app",
    "safe": false,
    "orphaned": true,
    "facts": {
      "size_bytes": 1048576
    }
  }
]`;
---

<Layout
  title="scan --json fields · lopper"
  description="Each field lopper scan --json prints, its type, when it is omitted, and what it means."
>
  <main>
    <section>
      <h1>scan --json</h1>
      <p class="lede dim">
        <code>lopper scan --json [path...]</code> prints a JSON array to stdout,
        one object per linked worktree in the order lopper found them, or{" "}
        <code>[]</code> when there are none. Main worktrees are not listed.
        Messages for a person go to stderr.
      </p>
      <pre><code>{example}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>worktree</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>
          path <span class="dim">string, always</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>The worktree's folder, as an absolute path.</dd>

        <dt>
          repo <span class="dim">string, always</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          The main worktree of the repository it belongs to, or the folder of a
          bare repository. For an orphaned worktree, where the repository was.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          branch <span class="dim">string, omitted if unknown</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          The branch checked out, such as <code>fix-login</code>. Omitted when
          HEAD is detached, or when lopper cannot tell, as for an orphaned
          worktree.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          safe <span class="dim">boolean, always</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Whether lopper considers it safe to delete. It is not safe when lopper
          could not check for work it holds. A <code>prunable</code> worktree is
          safe unless locked, since there is no folder left to lose.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          locked <span class="dim">boolean, omitted if false</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Someone ran <code>git worktree lock</code> on it. A locked worktree is
          never safe.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          prunable <span class="dim">boolean, omitted if false</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          The folder is gone and only Git's record of it is left.{" "}
          <code>git worktree prune</code> in the repository removes the record.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          orphaned <span class="dim">boolean, omitted if false</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          The folder is there, but its repository is gone or no longer lists it.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          moved_from <span class="dim">string, omitted unless moved</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Where Git still expects a worktree that was moved by hand.{" "}
          <code>git worktree repair</code> in the worktree fixes that.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          unconfirmed{" "}
          <span class="dim">string, omitted unless unconfirmed</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Why the repository named in the folder's <code>.git</code> file could
          not confirm the worktree, such as{" "}
          <code>gitdir is missing from …</code>.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          facts <span class="dim">object, always</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>What lopper found inside the worktree, described below.</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>facts</h2>
      <p class="intro dim">
        Each field is omitted when lopper does not know it: the check failed,
        and <code>errors</code> says why, or it did not run. lopper runs no Git
        checks on orphaned and prunable worktrees. A count of zero is printed as{" "}
        <code>0</code>, not omitted.
      </p>
      <dl>
        <dt>
          dirty <span class="dim">integer</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Entries <code>git status</code> lists: changed, staged and untracked.
          An untracked folder counts once.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          unchecked_files <span class="dim">integer</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Files whose assume-unchanged or skip-worktree index flag hides their
          edits from <code>git status</code>.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          unpushed <span class="dim">integer</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Commits on HEAD that are on no remote branch and not in the base
          branch, as of the last fetch.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          merged <span class="dim">string</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          <p>
            Whether the work reached the base branch: <code>origin/HEAD</code>,
            <code>main</code> or <code>master</code>. Also omitted when the
            repository has none of them.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <code>"ancestor"</code>: HEAD is in the base branch, by a merge or
              fast-forward.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code>"content"</code>: the base branch has the same changes,
              after a squash, rebase or cherry-pick.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code>"none"</code>: the work is not in the base branch.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </dd>

        <dt>
          size_bytes <span class="dim">integer</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          Total size of the regular files in the folder, or <code>0</code> when
          the folder is gone. Omitted when lopper could not measure the folder.
        </dd>

        <dt>
          errors <span class="dim">array of strings</span>
        </dt>
        <dd>
          One entry per failed check, such as{" "}
          <code>could not read status: …</code>. Omitted when no check failed.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lede {
    margin-top: 1lh;
    margin-bottom: 2lh;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1lh;
  }

  .intro {
    margin-bottom: 1.5lh;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  dt .dim {
    margin-left: 1ch;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  dt:not(:first-child) {
    margin-top: 1.5lh;
  }

  dd {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0.25lh 0 0 2.5ch;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  dd code {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0.5lh 0 0;
    padding-left: 2ch;
  }
</style>
